  "id": "4704e3db-62e6-4da9-aeaa-6dcc31721b8e",
  "title": "Ukraine and Russia: Zelensky and Trump’s Strategic Dynamics Amid Starlink and Energy Deals",
  "summary": "Ukraine President Volodymyr Zelensky criticized the U.S.-Russia diesel deal as a 'gift to Putin' while President Donald Trump defended the deal as a necessary step to secure energy supplies, amid growing tensions over Ukraine's military access to Starlink satellite internet. The Ukrainian leader accused the U.S. of picking the other side after four years of conflict.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Zelensky criticized Trump’s decision to waive Russia-related sanctions and tariffs as a 'gift to Putin' while Trump defended the deal as a necessary step to secure energy supplies.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Ukrainian leader accused the U.S. of picking the other side after four years of conflict.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Ukraine has been targeting Russia's oil industry for months, prompting fuel rationing and Moscow banning diesel exports, while the global crisis also came after the war on Iran curtailed oil shipments through the Strait of Hormuz.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
