      "title": "Many don't know what my decision is: Trump on Russia sanctions waiver",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/many-don-t-know-what-my-decision-is-trump-on-russia-sanctions-waiver-126101800091_1.html",
      "description": "Facing intense criticism, US President Donald Trump said he had taken a \"good decision\" to exempt Russia from sweeping sanctions under a new law and asserted that many did not know what it actually meant.\n\"A lot of you don't know what my decision is yet, but we'll figure it out, and you'll figure it out,\" Trump told reporters at the Mar-a-Lago resort in Miami on Saturday evening.\n\"It's a very good decision, and it's going to be a decision that's good for the country, and I think good for the world because we're really at a world stage,\" Trump said.\nOn Friday, Trump signed an executive order exempting Russia from a new sanctions measure  Graham Act  that the US Congress passed last month.\nThe executive order also granted a waiver from 100 per cent tariffs on the top five purchasers of Russian oil and gas, including China and India.\nThe order states that the waivers shall remain in effect until such time as the President or the Secretary of State, in consultation with the Secretary",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-18T04:38:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Zelenskyy criticizes Trump's waiver of sanctions on Russia as 'wrong'",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/zelenskyy-criticizes-trump-s-waiver-of-sanctions-on-russia-as-wrong-126101800071_1.html",
      "description": "Zelenskyy criticised US President Donald Trump's decision to waive Russia-related sanctions and tariffs, saying the move would encourage Moscow to continue attacks on Ukraine",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-18T02:39:49"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump wants 60 days to analyse impact of Russia sanctions law: Rubio",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/trump-wants-60-days-to-analyse-impact-of-russia-sanctions-law-rubio-126101800057_1.html",
      "description": "US President Donald Trump wants to take a 60-day period to analyse what imposing sanctions on Russia and tariffs on other countries would mean for the global economy, Secretary of State Marco Rubio said here.\nRubio was responding to questions on Saturday evening ahead of his departure for a week-long tour of Uzbekistan and India.\n\"I think the president wants to take the 60-day period of time to sort of analyse what imposing both sanctions and tariffs will mean to the global economy, and even to the US economy,\" Rubio said in response to a question on the waivers granted by Trump under the Sanctioning Russia and Iran Act or the Graham Act.\nOn Friday, Trump waived key provisions of the Graham Act that authorised punitive tariffs on countries purchasing Russian oil, offering relief to India.\nThe executive order signed by Trump on Friday states that the waivers shall remain in effect until such time as the President or the Secretary of State, in consultation with the Secretary of the .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-18T02:30:21"
    }
